      ],
      "text": "**Not clearly—Singapore looks at least as bad, and possibly worse in its western region.** At 11 p.m. on October 17, Johor Bahru’s reported US AQI was **235** (“very unhealthy”). Singapore’s latest readings, at midnight local time on October 18, showed **1-hour PM2.5 of 199 µg/m³ in the west**, with other regions lower. ([aqicn.org](https://aqicn.org/city/johor-bahru/))\n\nThose figures aren’t perfectly apples-to-apples: Johor’s is an AQI reading, while Singapore’s is a PM2.5 concentration. So the safest takeaway is that **both places have very poor air, and it doesn’t look like Johor Bahru is clearly worse right now**.([checkpointsg.com](https://www.checkpointsg.com/haze))",
